    "body": "The maintainer added this to the DXF work in chat on 2026-11-15.\n\nHis words: \"A DXF should be possible to \"place\" on a stock and used as references for cutting - not be treated like a model - thus for processes like wireedm, plasma, laser, etc etc.. we can just make a sheet, cube, cylinder. place the DXF - and select operations accordingly. The Adding DXF Profile, should thus live on \"Stock page\" and have a \"virtual\" model reference, just so the operations pages gets happy about a model being loaded..\"\n\nChange to the scope of this issue:\n\n1. The entry for a DXF profile is on the Stock page of the setup: a control \"Add DXF profile\". It is not `Model > Open`. Remove `.dxf` from the scope of `pick_mesh_file`.\n2. A `.dxf` file dropped on the viewport adds the profile to the active setup, through the same command. If no setup has a stock, the drop refuses with a message that tells the user to make a stock first.\n3. The Stock page lists the placed profiles of the setup, with the placement fields (position and rotation on the stock face), show/hide and delete. Each edit is a command.\n4. The viewport draws the sketch chains on the stock face where the profile is placed, not on the setup XY plane at Z 0.\n5. The operation pages accept a setup with a stock and a placed profile and no model (the virtual model reference of #1862). They do not show a \"no model\" refusal for the 2D operations on sketches.\n6. The missing-units prompt, the import summary, the browser row and the open-chain markers stay as the issue body says.\n\nDone means, in addition to the list in the issue body:\n\n- The user makes a stock (a sheet, a block or a cylinder) with no model, adds a DXF profile on the Stock page, and creates an operation on its chains.\n- Structural tests pin the Stock page control, the profile list and the operation page on a setup without a model.\n- The PR body has before and after screenshots.\n\nThe entity, command and virtual model reference are on #1862.\n",
